name: bitgarth-web
title: BitGarth
version: '@VERSION@'
summary: Private, self-hosted crypto portfolio tracker that runs in your browser
description: |
  BitGarth tracks your Bitcoin and Ethereum holdings without handing your
  financial data to a cloud service. It is watch-only: it syncs from public
  addresses and xpubs and never asks for seed phrases or private keys.

  This snap runs BitGarth as a background service on this machine. After
  installing, open http://127.0.0.1:8080 in a browser on the same computer.
  It listens only on this computer (loopback), not on your network.
  If port 8080 is taken, choose another: sudo snap set bitgarth-web port=8081
  Wallet data is stored encrypted under /var/snap/bitgarth-web/common.

  A command-line client is available separately as the bitgarth-cli snap.

  Website and documentation: https://bitgarth.app

  BitGarth is distributed under the FSL-1.1-ALv2 license.
license: Proprietary
website: https://bitgarth.app
source-code: https://github.com/BitGarth/bitgarth
base: core24
grade: stable
confinement: strict
platforms:
  amd64:
    build-on: [amd64]
    build-for: [amd64]
apps:
  bitgarth-web:
    command: bin/launch-web
    daemon: simple
    plugs: [network, network-bind]
    environment:
      LD_LIBRARY_PATH: "$SNAP/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu:$SNAP/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu"
      BITGARTH_CHANNEL: snap
parts:
  application:
    plugin: dump
    source: payload/
    stage-packages: [ca-certificates, libssl3t64]
  launcher:
    plugin: dump
    source: launcher/
    organize:
      launch-web: bin/launch-web
